<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Text To Word</title></head><body><h1>HalloweenVerse Feature Specification</h1>
<h2>1. Landing Page</h2>
<p>The landing page introduces the brand and directs users into the Halloween experience.</p>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Responsive navigation.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Animated hero section.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Interactive 3D environment.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Primary and secondary CTA buttons.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Feature discovery sections.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Educational content preview.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Game previews.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Celebration planner preview.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Event discovery preview.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Footer with useful navigation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All navigation links work.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>CTA buttons navigate to the correct destinations.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The page remains usable if 3D rendering fails.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>No horizontal overflow occurs on mobile.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>2. 3D Exploration</h2>
<p>Provide a navigable environment containing themed locations.</p>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Haunted mansion.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Pumpkin patch.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Trick-or-treat street.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Halloween carnival.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Halloween workshop.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Interactions:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Select locations by clicking.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Open information panels.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Return to the main map.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use keyboard and touch controls where applicable.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Every location has a working interaction.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Controls are clearly explained.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Loading and error states are implemented.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Users can exit the 3D experience easily.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. Educational Guide</h2>
<p>Provide structured content about Halloween's history, traditions, symbols, and contemporary celebrations.</p>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Searchable or navigable topics.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Readable content cards.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Sources for historical claims.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Practical Indian celebration examples.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content is accurate and understandable.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Historical claims are supported by credible references.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The page works without JavaScript-dependent decorative effects.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>4. Celebration Planner</h2>
<p>Inputs:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Celebration setting.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Number of participants.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Budget in INR.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Preferred atmosphere.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Available time.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Outputs:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Suggested activities.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Estimated costs.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Shopping or preparation checklist.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Suggested schedule.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Invalid inputs are handled.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Estimated totals are calculated correctly.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Total cost stays within the selected budget unless the user explicitly allows otherwise.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Users can reset and regenerate the plan.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>5. Costume Explorer</h2>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Costume cards.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Categories and filters.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Estimated budget.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Materials list.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Instructions.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Accessible image descriptions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Filters work correctly.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Empty results have a helpful message.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Images have appropriate alternative text.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>6. Games</h2>
<p>Initial games:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Pumpkin Carving Studio.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Spooky Memory Match.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Haunted House Challenge.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Controls work on touchscreens and desktops.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Scores and completion states are accurate.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Restart and reset work.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>No game requires a user account.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>7. Event Explorer</h2>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Event cards.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>City and category filters.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Date and price information.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Organizer details.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Registration links.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Last-verified date.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Acceptance criteria:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Unverified events are not published as confirmed.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>External links are clearly identified.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Empty search results are handled.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Expired events are marked or removed.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Sample events are clearly identified in development environments.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>8. Global Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Consistent navigation.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Responsive layouts.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Loading, error, and empty states.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Keyboard-accessible interactions.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Reduced-motion support.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Basic SEO.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Performance monitoring.</p>
</li>
</ul></body></html>